! ISOMIP+ Ocean0, IDEALISED draft, on the QUASI-GEOPOTENTIAL coordinate
! with basal melt and ice-shelf top drag ON.
!
! This is `ocean0_idealised_draft.nml` with `vcoord_type = "z_fixed"` +
! `zfixed_closed_faces`, and nothing else changed except what that
! coordinate forces (`h_min_cavity >= 2*h_nominal`) and the measurement
! horizon.  It is the payoff case of the shared first-live-layer index
! `k_top`: under a z-like coordinate the layers inside the ice draft are
! inert fillers, so `k = nz` is NOT the ice-adjacent layer, and until
! `k_top` landed `validate_config` refused `&ocean_cavity_melt_nml
! enable`, `&ocean_tdrag_nml enable` and `&ocean_hdiff_nml kappa_h /= 0`
! here -- the melt deposit would have been frozen on a massless filler by
! the vdiff decoupling gate, then deleted by the ALE remap drain, with
! the console budget still counting it.
!
! The melt-OFF twin of this configuration is measured in
! `cavity_rest_growth_diagnosis.md` section Y.1 and carries a spurious
! growing mode (En 6.9E-09 at day 1 -> 1.3E-06 at day 30, exponential
! after day 15 on a ~4.2-day e-folding, seeded at the partial cells by
! the partial-step PGF quadrature error).  That mode is NOT a melt
! problem and is owned elsewhere; read this case's energy against that
! baseline, not against zero.
!
!
! ================ MEASURED, 30 days, melt ON =====================
!
! nvfortran 25.5 `-stdpar=gpu` cc70, one V100: 30 days in 164 s
! (5.5 s / simulated day).  gfortran 15.1 Release agrees to every
! printed digit at every daily checkpoint it was carried to.
! Zero `[nan-catch]` lines, zero CFL truncations, `MaxCFL <= 0.0662`.
! `melt` columns: 2584 covered, the same count `configure_ocean_k_top`
! reports as carrying top-side fillers.
!
!  day | En (m2/s2) | MaxCFL | max|u| | melt mean / max / min (m/yr) | Mass Err | Salt Err | Heat Err
!  ----|------------|--------|--------|------------------------------|----------|----------|---------
!    1 |  7.442E-08 | 0.0016 | 2.2e-3 |   3.77 /   8.66 /  +1.01     | -1.9E-14 |  2.1E-14 | -1.6E-14
!    5 |  2.999E-06 | 0.0115 | 5.6e-2 |   4.99 /  27.61 /  +0.84     | -9.7E-14 |  1.0E-13 | -1.2E-13
!   10 |  2.628E-05 | 0.0285 | 1.7e-1 |   5.67 /  29.72 /  +0.69     | -1.9E-13 |  2.1E-13 | -3.3E-13
!   20 |  1.433E-04 | 0.0513 | 2.9e-1 |   6.08 /  35.64 /  -1.01     | -3.9E-13 | -4.3E-09 |  6.0E-09
!   30 |  3.302E-04 | 0.0621 | 2.4e-1 |   7.83 /  65.92 /  -0.70     | -5.8E-13 | -5.5E-08 |  8.0E-08
!
! (melt statistics are over the COVERED columns only — every cavity
! diagnostic is NaN outside the cover — and are sampled at the half-day
! the daily diagnostic fires.  A NEGATIVE melt rate is refreezing; it
! first appears on day 13.)
!
! READ THE BUDGETS HONESTLY.  Through day 15 all three residuals grow
! LINEARLY with step count at ~2E-14/day, which is round-off
! accumulation and nothing else.  At day 16 the salt and heat residuals
! JUMP four decades and change sign, reaching 5.5E-08 / 8.0E-08 relative
! by day 30 — still only 2E-05 of the tracked melt source, and nothing
! like the per-step leak of the WHOLE deposit that the pre-k_top
! refusal named, but NOT round-off.  It was not isolated.  The leading
! suspect is the BED side, which Phase 6 scoped out on purpose: `k_bot`
! was deliberately not shipped, the partial BOTTOM cell absorbs eta plus
! the bed fillers' debt and the closed-faces census measured the
! thinnest live layer on this geometry at 1.8 mm, so once the flow is
! energetic enough to move it through `H_VANISHED` the ALE remap drain
! empties it un-budgeted.  Do not quote this case's budgets as closed
! past day 15.
!
! The ENERGY is the melt-driven circulation, not a spurious mode: the
! melt-OFF twin of this configuration sits at En = 1.3E-06 at day 30
! (`cavity_rest_growth_diagnosis.md` section Y.1) and this run is 250x
! that, with max|u| ~ 25 cm/s plume velocities in the right places.
! The sigma twin of THIS case (same namelist, `vcoord_type = "sigma"`,
! `h_min_cavity = 20`) does not survive: it blows the barotropic loop up
! on day 3 and `validate_config`'s melt solver fails loud on 1413
! non-finite columns.  That contrast is the point of the coordinate.
!
! The IDEALISED draft (analytic, no external data) is the same one
! `ocean0_idealised_draft.nml` uses; its derivation follows.
!
! Asay-Davis, Cornford, Durand, Galton-Fenzi, Gladstone, Gudmundsson,
! Hattermann, Holland, Holland, Holland, Martin, Mathiot, Pattyn and
! Seroussi (2016), "Experimental design for three interrelated marine ice
! sheet and ocean model intercomparison projects", Geosci. Model Dev. 9,
! 2471-2497, doi:10.5194/gmd-9-2471-2016.  Ocean0: WARM initial
! condition, WARM far-field restoring, static topography (their Table 2 +
! Sect. 3.2.1).
!
! WHAT IS IDEALISED, AND WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  The protocol's ice draft
! is NOT analytic — Sect. 3.1.1 says so outright ("Because the ice-draft
! topography is derived from ice-sheet model results, it cannot be
! described by an analytic function") and ships it as BISICLES NetCDF
! (Cornford and Asay-Davis 2016).  `ocean0.nml` reads that file.  THIS
! file replaces it with a linear-in-x draft anchored on the two numbers
! the paper does print, so the configuration can be exercised end to end
! with nothing to download:
!
!   * the steady-state GROUNDING LINE crosses the centreline of the
!     trough at x = 450 +/- 10 km (their Sect. 2.1);
!   * the CALVING FRONT is at x_calve = 640 km, where ice thinner than
!     H_calve = 100 m -- "equivalent to an ice draft above ~ -90 m"
!     (Sect. 3.1.2) -- has been removed.
!
! Fitting a straight line through (450 km, 600 m) and (640 km, 90 m)
! gives d(draft)/dx = -2.6842e-3, and anchoring it at x0 = -10 km of
! MODEL x (i.e. 310 km of paper x, outside the domain) puts 975.79 m
! there.  West of the grounding line the formula is deeper than the bed,
! so those columns ground through the ordinary `h_min_cavity` path and
! become land -- which is what "grounded ice sheet" means here.  Measured
! at configure: the trough-centre grounding line lands at x = 449 km, the
! draft at the calving front is exactly 90.0 m, and 3778 of 9600 interior
! columns (39.4 %) ground.
!
! EVERYTHING ELSE follows the protocol.  See ../isomip_plus/README.md for
! the full parameter-by-parameter mapping, including the rows this build
! cannot honour (no-slip walls, real freshwater mass flux, under-ice u*
! in the boundary-layer scheme).
!
! t_end below is the PROTOCOL duration (Sect. 3.2.1: quasi-equilibrium
! plus 6 months, expected 1-2 years).  For a smoke test, override it:
!     ./build/rdb <this file>            # the real thing
!   with `&time_nml t_end = 86400.0 /` appended, one simulated day.

&sim_nml
   sim_type = "ocean"
/

&grid_nml
   ! 480 km x 80 km at the COM resolution (Table 3 Lx/Ly, Table 4 dx=dy).
   nx     = 240
   ny     = 40
   dx     = 2000.0
   dy     = 2000.0
   nghost = 2
/

&time_nml
   t_end        = 2592000.0    ! 30 days -- the horizon of the z_fixed
                               ! measurement (the protocol's own duration
                               ! is 1 year; see the header)
   dt_fixed     = 300.0
   cfl_interval = 1
/

&physics_nml
   ! f-plane at 75 S (Sect. 3.1.1): f = -2*Omega*sin(75 deg).
   coriolis_f    = -1.409e-4
   wind_stress_x = 0.0         ! "There is no forcing at the surface of the
   wind_stress_y = 0.0         !  open ocean" (Sect. 3.1.3)
/

&nonhydrostatic_nml
   nz_layers = 36              ! Sect. 3.1.5: "all models should have 36
                               ! vertical layers", distribution at the
                               ! modeller's discretion
/

&vcoord_nml
   ! THE CASE UNDER TEST: quasi-geopotential layers under the shelf.
   ! h_nominal = &ocean_topo_nml max_depth / nz = 720/36 = 20 m, which is
   ! the protocol's own 36 x 20 m stack with no second spelling.  The
   ! layers whose nominal range lies inside the ice draft become inert
   ! fillers at zstar_h_min; `k_top` is what keeps every top-side
   ! consumer off them (P6.3/P6.4).
   vcoord_type         = "z_fixed"
   zfixed_closed_faces = .true.   ! partial steps: a face whose layer is a
                                  ! filler on either side is a z-level WALL
                                  ! (Adcroft, Hill & Marshall 1997; Losch
                                  ! 2008 section 2.1).  Also what makes
                                  ! kappa_h legal here — every face
                                  ! touching a filler carries zero flux.
   ! I1 tripwire: this coordinate vanishes layers, so assert once per
   ! outer step that no layer at or below H_VANISHED holds tracer
   ! content (src/core/ocean/README.md, the vanished-layer content rule).
   check_vanished_content = .true.
/

&ocean_topo_nml
   topo_config    = "isomip_plus"   ! Eqs. (1)-(4) + Table 1
   max_depth      = 720.0           ! = -z_b,deep, the Eq. (1) deep clip
   x_origin       = 320000.0        ! Table 3 x0: the ocean box starts at
                                    ! x = 320 km on the MISMIP+ axis
   wind_config    = "constant"
   taux_magnitude = 0.0
   coriolis_beta  = 0.0
   coriolis_y_ref = 0.0
/

&ocean_cavity_dyn_nml
   enable       = .true.
   draft_config = "linear"     ! the idealised stand-in; ocean0.nml reads the file
   draft_depth  = 975.79       ! draft AT draft_x0
   draft_slope  = -2.6842e-3   ! (90 - 600)/(640 - 450) km, shallowing seaward
   draft_x0     = -10000.0     ! anchor OUTSIDE the domain so the ghosts are iced
   draft_x1     = 320000.0     ! x_calve = 640 km in model x; open ocean beyond
   h_min_cavity = 40.0         ! = 2*h_nominal, which validate_config
                               ! REQUIRES under z_fixed and which is
                               ! ISOMIP+ Sect. 3.1.5's own rule
                               ! ("approximately two grid cells, ~40 m if
                               ! z levels are equally spaced").  NOTE it
                               ! moves the grounding line relative to the
                               ! sigma leg -- 3912 of 9600 interior
                               ! columns ground here vs 3778 -- a confound
                               ! the coordinate study must control for.
/

&ocean_cavity_melt_nml
   enable          = .true.
   exchange_law    = "const_gamma"   ! Sect. 3.1.8: three-equation, constant
                                     ! Gamma_T/Gamma_S
   gamma_t         = 2.2e-2          ! Sect. 3.2.1 starting guess
                                     ! (St = sqrt(C_D)*Gamma_T = 1.1e-3)
   gamma_s         = -1.0            ! < 0 => derived as Gamma_T/35 (Table 4)
   cdrag_top       = 2.5e-3          ! Table 4 C_D,top; must match &ocean_tdrag_nml cd
   u_tide          = 1.0e-2          ! Table 4 u_tidal (melt u* only, never the drag)
   ice_conduction  = "insulating"    ! Table 4 kappa_i = 0
   s_ice           = 0.0             ! Table 4 / Sect. 3.1.8
   far_field_depth = 10.0            ! METRES below the ice base; the protocol
                                     ! leaves the method to the modeller
                                     ! (Sect. 3.1.8) and asks it be documented
/

&ocean_tdrag_nml
   enable = .true.
   form   = "quadratic"
   cd     = 2.5e-3             ! Table 4 C_D,top
/

&ocean_bdrag_nml
   form = "quadratic"
   cd   = 2.5e-3               ! Table 4 C_D,bot
/

&ocean_forcing_nml
   enable_components = .true.  ! required by the melt path (it owns two
                               ! surface-flux components)
/

&ocean_pgf_nml
   form        = "fv_mom6"     ! the only form with an injectable top BC
   p_top_in_bc = .true.        ! REQUIRED for a varying draft
   maxvel      = 5.0
/

&ocean_eos_nml
   eos          = "linear"     ! Sect. 3.1.7 / Eq. (23)
   tfreeze_set  = "isomip"     ! Table 4 lambda1/2/3, used by Eq. (25)
/

&ocean_ic_nml
   ! Roundabout's alpha_T/beta_S are DIMENSIONAL (kg/m3 per unit) whereas
   ! the protocol's alpha_lin/beta_lin are FRACTIONAL (they multiply
   ! rho_ref inside the bracket of Eq. 23).  Feeding the fractional
   ! numbers straight in under-states the density response ~1000x and
   ! looks like a plausible weak run.
   alpha_T = 3.8356948e-2      ! rho_ref * 3.733e-5 /degC   (Table 4)
   beta_S  = 8.0587609e-1      ! rho_ref * 7.843e-4 /PSU    (Table 4)
   T_ref   = -1.0              ! Table 4 T_ref
   S_ref   = 34.2              ! Table 4 S_ref
   rho_0   = 1027.51           ! Table 4 rho_ref
/

&ocean_zinit_nml
   ! WARM initial condition, Eqs. (21)-(22) + Table 6, written in the
   ! z-positive-UP convention.  NOTE the printed Eq. (22) has a typo
   ! (`S0 + (S_bot - T0)*z/z_b,deep`); it must be `(S_bot - S0)`.
   !   T: -1.9 degC at z = 0  ->  +1.0 degC at z = -720 m
   !      dT/dz = -(1.0 - (-1.9))/720 = -4.0277778e-3  (WARM is thermally
   !      UNSTABLE -- CDW at depth -- stabilised by the salinity gradient)
   !   S: 33.8 PSU at z = 0   ->  34.7 PSU at z = -720 m
   !      dS/dz = -(34.7 - 33.8)/720 = -1.25e-3
   enable    = .true.
   source    = "linear"        ! analytic T(z)/S(z) at the TRUE geopotential
                               ! depth (column top at z = -z_draft), so the
                               ! isopycnals are flat in z under a tilted lid
   lin_t_ref = -1.9
   lin_dt_dz = -4.0277778e-3
   lin_s_ref = 33.8
   lin_ds_dz = -1.25e-3
/

&tracer_nml
   ! Overwritten everywhere by the zinit overlay; kept consistent so a
   ! reader is not misled about what is seeded.
   initial_temperature = -0.45
   initial_salinity    = 34.25
/

&ocean_bc_nml
   ! "the only forcing is via 3-D restoring within 10 km of the northern
   !  boundary" (Sect. 3.1.3).  The paper's +x is north; in model terms
   !  that is the EAST edge.  OBC_SPONGE leaves the edge itself a WALL
   !  (it is not a tracer-open type) and adds the interior relaxation
   !  band -- which is exactly the protocol's "northern wall adjacent to
   !  the restoring region" (Sect. 3.1.4).
   west  = "wall"
   east  = "sponge"
   south = "wall"
   north = "wall"
   sponge_width    = 5           ! (x_r1 - x_r0)/dx = 10 km / 2 km, Table 3
   sponge_strength = 1.1574074e-4  ! gamma0 = 10 day^-1 = 10/86400 s^-1
/

&ocean_sponge_nml
   ! Ocean0 restores to the WARM profile it was initialised with, so
   ! target_source="ic" would give the same answer here -- linear_z is
   ! used anyway so Ocean0/1/2 differ by their profile numbers ALONE and
   ! nothing else in the file has to change.
   enable        = .true.
   damp_source   = "band"
   ramp          = "linear"      ! Eq. (20): gamma rises linearly from 0 at
                                 ! x_r0 = 790 km to gamma0 at x_r1 = 800 km
   target_source = "linear_z"
   relax_uv      = .false.       ! Eqs. (18)-(19) restore T and S only
   relax_tracers = .true.
   lin_t_ref     = -1.9          ! WARM restoring (Table 6), as above
   lin_dt_dz     = -4.0277778e-3
   lin_s_ref     = 33.8
   lin_ds_dz     = -1.25e-3
/

&ocean_coriolis_nml
   form = "sadourny"
/

&ocean_hvisc_nml
   nu_h = 6.0                  ! Table 4 nu_H (harmonic, constant)
   nu_4 = 0.0
/

&ocean_hdiff_nml
   ! Table 4 kappa_H is 1.0, and with zfixed_closed_faces on it is legal
   ! here.  It is set to ZERO anyway so this run is directly comparable
   ! with the melt-OFF z_fixed twin measured in
   ! cavity_rest_growth_diagnosis.md section Y.1, which had to run at 0
   ! because kappa_h was refused outright.  Restore 1.0 to run the
   ! protocol.
   kappa_h = 0.0
/

&ocean_vmix_nml
   ! Sect. 3.1.6 asks for CONSTANT vertical viscosity/diffusivity.  PP81
   ! with nu0 = 0 degenerates to exactly that: kv == pp81_nu_bg and
   ! kt == ks == pp81_kappa_bg at every interface, with no Richardson
   ! dependence left.  KPP is off for the same reason -- the protocol
   ! prescribes harmonic diffusion with fixed coefficients, and a
   ! boundary-layer scheme would be a different experiment.
   use_closure   = .true.
   use_kpp       = .false.
   pp81_nu0      = 0.0
   pp81_nu_bg    = 1.0e-3      ! Table 4 nu_stab
   pp81_kappa_bg = 5.0e-5      ! Table 4 kappa_stab
/

&ocean_conv_nml
   ! Table 4 nu_unstab = kappa_unstab = 0.1 m2/s, applied "when the local
   ! stratification is unstable" (Sect. 3.1.6).
   enable       = .true.
   kd_conv      = 0.1
   prandtl_conv = 1.0          ! Kv_conv = Kd_conv
   n2_thresh    = 0.0          ! trigger on N^2 < 0
/

&ocean_bt_nml
   auto_n_inner = .true.
   ! split_scheme left at the default pred_corr (the protocol says nothing
   ! about the outer time split).
/

&ocean_diag_nml
   enabled  = .true.
   filename = "isomip_ocean0_idealised_zfixed"
   dt_out   = 86400.0          ! daily
   ! The cavity melt fields are derived-catalog entries (opt-in).  Named
   ! here so the payoff run reports the mean and max melt rate in the
   ! ISOMIP+ convention (m/yr of ice) alongside the energy and the
   ! budgets.  Every one is NaN outside the cover, so a domain mean over
   ! the output is a mean over the CAVITY.
   diags    = "melt_m_per_yr  melt  thermal_driving"
/

&output_nml
   output_dir     = "./out_isomip_ocean0_idealised_zfixed"
   output_to_file = .false.
/

&logging_nml
   log_level       = "info"
   status_interval = 86400.0
/
